From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: one type scale and dock-tile geometry across shelf islands

The live extension, the media player and the clock each set their own
text sizes -- six between them -- so an event title, a song title and the
time never agreed. Titles and times are now 12px and what describes them
10px. The calendar badge and album artwork are 36px squares with the dock
icon's corner radius, and every island insets its content by the dock's
10px.

Opening from the shelf now asks the Shell to activate the application.
A D-Bus raise or a launch without an activation token only produced an
"is ready" notification on Wayland: the media player did not come
forward and a live extension's application stayed behind. A live
extension's passive open action is invoked as well, so the application
can show what was clicked.

